{
    "word": "uproarious",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "3c79f1d2-53f1-3249-a5eb-302939d16fc8",
                "word": "uproarious",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "e5dc7437-707d-41f5-91c0-26857c9629e0",
                        "entry_id": "3c79f1d2-53f1-3249-a5eb-302939d16fc8",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more uproarious"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "dce323e7-347a-4d3a-9fa5-926f5739c67d",
                        "entry_id": "3c79f1d2-53f1-3249-a5eb-302939d16fc8",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most uproarious"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9783afea-25e9-3a18-9984-b7f7054e854e",
                        "entry_id": "3c79f1d2-53f1-3249-a5eb-302939d16fc8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Causing, or likely to cause, an uproar."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "da1f1672-a0c0-462a-807d-0fcb1e77550b",
                                "sense_id": "9783afea-25e9-3a18-9984-b7f7054e854e",
                                "text": "“Oh! there's no fear of him,” said Burgess, cheerily; “if he grows uproarious, we'll soon give him a touch of the cat.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b11791fa-040e-3680-a5a5-dbf31ac52139",
                        "entry_id": "3c79f1d2-53f1-3249-a5eb-302939d16fc8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Characterized by uproar, that is, loud, confused noise, or by noisy and uncontrollable laughter."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e22674ed-f64a-411f-8cc9-119e0a495273",
                                "sense_id": "b11791fa-040e-3680-a5a5-dbf31ac52139",
                                "text": "The noise in this room was perfectly tumultuous, […] every child was conducting itself like forty. The consequences were uproarious beyond belief; but no one seemed to care; on the contrary, the mother and daughter laughed heartily, and enjoyed it very much; and the latter, soon beginning to mingle in the sports, got pillaged by the young brigands most ruthlessly."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "978e8ce7-0e3d-4b97-9db1-3c0a27d0e5cf",
                                "sense_id": "b11791fa-040e-3680-a5a5-dbf31ac52139",
                                "text": "One \"set\" off, another takes its place, he or she remaining longest on the floor receiving the most uproarious commendation, and so the dancing continues until broad daylight. It does not cease with the sound of the fiddle, but in that case they set up a music peculiar to themselves."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "de7bb328-28d4-4ac7-a024-cd896dc5acd0",
                                "sense_id": "b11791fa-040e-3680-a5a5-dbf31ac52139",
                                "text": "The two bushes looked up in surprise, and when they saw Dorothy, the Cowardly Lion and Sir Hokus, they fell into each other's branches and burst into the most uproarious laughter."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "85ed19f0-1f35-455d-a2a6-453e07fe6431",
                                "sense_id": "b11791fa-040e-3680-a5a5-dbf31ac52139",
                                "text": "At the uproarious cheering which greeted his appearance, [Maximilien] Robespierre advanced into the open, whilst a sudden swift light of triumph darted from his narrow, pale eyes."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "696b6377-85a5-3d8c-80cf-49f24516a1fc",
                        "entry_id": "3c79f1d2-53f1-3249-a5eb-302939d16fc8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Extremely funny; hilarious."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c1c62fe0-f9a2-46ce-a060-17e5fc3d3e4f",
                                "sense_id": "696b6377-85a5-3d8c-80cf-49f24516a1fc",
                                "text": "Yet as with Booksmart, the summer's earlier riff on that Apatovian classic, there are times when Good Boys feels a little too nice to actually be uproarious. In more ways than one, it's the training wheels for a better comedy—a slightly edgier and funnier one."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9fb9f2cc-c86d-36de-a64a-63e189c05c61",
                        "entry_id": "3c79f1d2-53f1-3249-a5eb-302939d16fc8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In a mess; dishevelled, untidy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c10bc24f-81bd-48d1-b8a9-10c1064da4be",
                        "source_entry_id": "3c79f1d2-53f1-3249-a5eb-302939d16fc8",
                        "source_sense_description": "characterised by uproar, that is, loud, confused noise, or by noisy and uncontrollable laughter",
                        "target_lang_word": "tumultueux",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tumultueux",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d7abfd83-6bc0-3e9e-993e-5b56216e4333",
                                        "entry_id": "86805238-b09c-37c5-a2fd-c3703ee04ed2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui se fait avec tumulte, avec confusion et bruit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "356a60c3-ce1c-4f95-aea2-9c6497c05c14",
                                                "sense_id": "d7abfd83-6bc0-3e9e-993e-5b56216e4333",
                                                "text": "Tumultueux concours de monde aux abords de l’embarcadère, gens qui partent et gens qui regardent partir, recrutés parmi la population cosmopolite de Bakou."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d367e08b-6245-4140-b584-0b9ae2b74881",
                                                "sense_id": "d7abfd83-6bc0-3e9e-993e-5b56216e4333",
                                                "text": "Loin de vouloir se livrer à une démonstration tumultueuse, la population fourmisienne ne songe qu'à célébrer les Pâques fleuries du 1ᵉʳ mai."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "99ec3095-6679-49f3-8ba9-f5b5819a0a1d",
                                                "sense_id": "d7abfd83-6bc0-3e9e-993e-5b56216e4333",
                                                "text": "Le troupeau n'en finissait plus. Quand il disparut au bout de la rue, il me sembla qu'elle était encore pleine des bœufs saugrenus qui passaient comme un fleuve avec leurs dos tumultueux."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af52c07f-160a-49ef-92a7-02f0c8adc2e5",
                                                "sense_id": "d7abfd83-6bc0-3e9e-993e-5b56216e4333",
                                                "text": "— […] : les jours de grande pluie, nous lancions sur les flots tumultueux des caniveaux le cuirassé « Suffren » fait d'une boîte à sardines, marque « A la Rose », le couvercle spiraleux disposé comme une voile […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3206ffd7-0422-36b8-a0b3-07fe4aaaf084",
                                        "entry_id": "86805238-b09c-37c5-a2fd-c3703ee04ed2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui donne une impression de désordre."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e81de904-caec-46ff-9728-6cead2234284",
                                                "sense_id": "3206ffd7-0422-36b8-a0b3-07fe4aaaf084",
                                                "text": "Le manteau noir qui la recouvrait s’ouvrait sur un corsage sombre, simple, presque de bon goût ; par contre, son chapeau tumultueux quoique noir la signalait d’une manière désobligeante."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e077c942-4d40-419d-9df0-58a9b9fcce60",
                        "source_entry_id": "3c79f1d2-53f1-3249-a5eb-302939d16fc8",
